1,2908,1246,279,2849,315,279,2003,10775,1449,220,22,2849,323,1221,990,279,1995,429,220,17,15,15,2849,614,5823,382,5338,11,582,1477,279,26313,979,220,17,15,15,374,17779,553,220,22,11,1576,279,2849,315,279,2003,13153,1449,220,22,2849,13,1096,646,387,2814,1667,279,59864,5666,1447,78045,220,17,15,15,1124,611,220,22,284,220,17,23,1124,1318,90,26313,335,220,19,1124,21675,522,37420,91339,29,151645,198,151644,872,198,2610,1231,312,18883,55856,279,3491,323,18130,279,6291,504,279,7167,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nKim's birthday was 200 days ago. Today is Wednesday. On what day of the week did his birthday fall?\n\nPartial draft:\n<partial_draft>\nTo determine the day of the week for Kim's birthday, we need to work backwards from today, which is Wednesday. We need to consider how the days of the week cycle every 7 days and then use the information that 200 days have passed.\n\nFirst, we find the remainder when 200 is divided by 7, because the days of the week repeat every 7 days. This can be done using the modulo operation:\n\n\\[ 200 \\div 7 = 28 \\text{ remainder } 4 \\]\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"You may re-analyze the problem and rewrite the solution from the beginning.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"3c073fa30d89e44c13ff6af62b69035a7efd45d0396274814fa1fb2905687ae3"},"seconds":13.314696073532104,"seed":1080035111652442369,"stop":"eos","text":"To determine the day of the week on which Kim's birthday fell, we need to work backward from today, which is a Wednesday, by 200 days. Since the days of the week repeat every 7 days, we can simplify our calculation by finding the remainder when 200 is divided by 7.\n\nFirst, we perform the division:\n\n\\[ 200 \\div 7 = 28 \\text{ remainder } 4 \\]\n\nThis tells us that 200 days is equivalent to 28 full weeks plus 4 extra days. Since 28 weeks is exactly 4 full cycles of the week, we only need to count back 4 days from Wednesday to find the day of the week for Kim's birthday.\n\nCounting back from Wednesday:\n\n1. One day before Wednesday is Tuesday.\n2. Two days before Wednesday is Monday.\n3. Three days before Wednesday is Sunday.\n4. Four days before Wednesday is Saturday.\n\nTherefore, Kim's birthday fell on a \\(\\boxed{\\text{Saturday}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\text{Saturday}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To determine the day of the week on which Kim's birthday fell, we need to work backward from today, which is a Wednesday, by 200 days. Since the days of the week repeat every 7 days, we can simplify our calculation by finding the remainder when 200 is divided by 7.\n\nFirst, we perform the division:\n\n\\[ 200 \\div 7 = 28 \\text{ remainder } 4 \\]\n\nThis tells us that 200 days is equivalent to 28 full weeks plus 4 extra days. Since 28 weeks is exactly 4 full cycles of the week, we only need to count back 4 days from Wednesday to find the day of the week for Kim's birthday.\n\nCounting back from Wednesday:\n\n1. One day before Wednesday is Tuesday.\n2. Two days before Wednesday is Monday.\n3. Three days before Wednesday is Sunday.\n4. Four days before Wednesday is Saturday.\n\nTherefore, Kim's birthday fell on a \\(\\boxed{\\text{Saturday}}\\).","id":"number_theory:49"}
